Wishly — Wishlist App for Shopify
Wishly is a wishlist application for Shopify that allows shoppers to save products they love and return to them later.

It supports both guest visitors and logged-in customers while providing merchants with a Shopify-native wishlist experience.

Status: 🚧 Currently under active development. Core guest and customer wishlist flows are working; production hardening and App Store release are in progress.

✨ Features
❤️ Add/remove products from wishlist

👤 Guest wishlist support (localStorage)

🔐 Logged-in customer wishlists (Prisma-backed API)

💾 Persistent customer wishlist storage

🔢 Wishlist counter

🛍️ Product card wishlist buttons

📄 Dedicated wishlist page

🎨 Theme App Extension integration

⚡ Asynchronous wishlist updates

📱 Responsive storefront support

🔄 Guest-to-customer synchronization (planned)

🏗️ Architecture
Wishly uses different storage strategies depending on the customer state.

Guest Customers
text
Storefront
    ↓
Wishly
    ↓
Browser Storage (localStorage)
Guest wishlists are stored locally in the customer's browser under the key wishly_wishlist. No API or database call is required for guest operations.

Logged-In Customers
text
Storefront
    ↓
Wishly API
    ↓
Prisma ORM
    ↓
Application Database
Logged-in customers receive a persistent wishlist associated with their Shopify customer ID.

Customer identity is detected via Shopify Liquid:

liquid
<script>
  window.WishlyCustomer = {
    loggedIn: {% if customer %}true{% else %}false{% endif %},
    id: {% if customer %}"{{ customer.id }}"{% else %}null{% endif %}
  };
</script>
