🚀 Getting Started
Requirements
Before starting, make sure you have:

Node.js (v20+)

npm

Shopify CLI

A Shopify Partner account

A Shopify development store

Install Dependencies
bash
npm install
Generate Prisma Client
bash
npx prisma generate
Run Database Migrations
bash
npx prisma migrate dev
Start Development
bash
shopify app dev
Follow the Shopify CLI instructions to install and preview the app on your development store.

🗄️ Database
Wishly uses Prisma for database access. Development currently uses SQLite; production will use PostgreSQL.

Wishlist Model
prisma
model Wishlist {
  id         String   @id @default(cuid())
  customerId String   @unique
  shop       String
  items      Json
  createdAt  DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt  DateTime @updatedAt
}
Each logged-in customer has one wishlist record per shop.

Example record:

json
{
  "customerId": "9259301699819",
  "shop": "example.myshopify.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "9105835557099",
      "handle": "vanilla-candle",
      "addedAt": "2026-09-06T20:43:21.047Z"
    }
  ]
}
🔌 Wishlist API
The wishlist API route is:

text
/api/wishlist
GET Wishlist
text
GET /api/wishlist?customerId=9259301699819
Example response:

json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Wishlist retrieved successfully",
  "wishlist": {
    "id": "wishlist_id",
    "customerId": "9259301699819",
    "shop": "example.myshopify.com",
    "items": [
      {
        "productId": "9105835557099",
        "handle": "vanilla-candle",
        "addedAt": "2026-09-06T20:43:21.047Z"
      }
    ]
  }
}
POST Wishlist
text
POST /api/wishlist
Body:

json
{
  "customerId": "9259301699819",
  "shop": "example.myshopify.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "9105835557099",
      "handle": "vanilla-candle",
      "addedAt": "2026-09-06T20:43:21.047Z"
    }
  ]
}
The API uses Prisma upsert() so the wishlist is created or updated.

🌐 Storefront JavaScript API
The Theme App Extension exposes a global JavaScript API on window.Wishly:

js
window.Wishly.getWishlist();
window.Wishly.getGuestWishlist();
window.Wishly.getCustomerWishlist();
window.Wishly.addToWishlist(productId, handle);
window.Wishly.removeFromWishlist(productId);
window.Wishly.toggleWishlist(productId, handle);
window.Wishly.updateButtons();
window.Wishly.updateCounter();
Check customer state:

js
window.Wishly.isLoggedIn
❤️ Storefront Wishlist Button
Products expose a wishlist button using data attributes:

liquid
<button
  type="button"
  class="wishly-heart-button"
  data-wishly-product="{{ product.id }}"
  data-wishly-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
  aria-label="Add {{ product.title | escape }} to wishlist"
>
  <span class="wishly-heart">♡</span>
</button>
Wishly automatically detects buttons containing data-wishly-product. The heart toggles between ♡ and ♥ based on wishlist state.

🔢 Wishlist Counter
Wishlist counters use:

html
<span data-wishly-counter>0</span>
Wishly automatically updates all elements with data-wishly-counter whenever the wishlist changes.

📄 Wishlist Page
The Theme App Extension includes a dedicated wishlist page section.

js
const wishlist = await window.Wishly?.getWishlist() || [];
Because getWishlist() is asynchronous, it must be called with await.

